["home/mistakes/streaky-windows-sunlight","Why The Streaks Come Back","Streaks return because the glass dries before the squeegee finishes: sunlight, over-soaped water and a saturated cloth are the three causes, and they stack. The professional's schedule follows the shade across the house, and the solution barely foams.","The evaporation race","Hot glass dries the solution mid-pass.","The soap trap","Foam leaves film; two drops per bucket is plenty.","Cloth discipline","One clean edge per pane, folded often.","The tool choice","Small squeegees control their corners better.","The finish pass","A dry microfibre edge catches the last line.","The season plan","Harmattan dust demands more frequent, lighter cleans.","Window cleaning rewards patience with the weather more than effort with the cloth. Cut the soap, chase the shade, and keep the rubber sharp: the streaks are a drying-time problem, and the fix is scheduling.","x"],
["entertainment/best-films-for-a-group","What Makes A Crowd-Pleaser","The best group films share three traits: a hook anyone can describe in one sentence, momentum that survives conversation and a runtime that respects the evening. The picks here were chosen for rooms that talk during movies.","One-sentence hooks","If the premise needs a paragraph, the room drifts.","Runtime discipline","Two hours is the group-watching ceiling.","Chatty-proof plots","Clear stakes keep commentary from derailing the story.","The comfort currency","Rewatches are the safest bets on mixed shelves.","The pick rule","Choose before the group assembles.","Momentum beats prestige in every group setting: the film that keeps a talking room oriented is doing harder work than the masterpiece that demands silence.","x"],
["fitness/dumbbell-only-home-programme-explained","How The Programme Progresses","The programme progresses on three levers: reps before load, load before density, and density before variety. Home trainees who chase variety plateau; trainees who add one rep per week keep arriving.","Reps first","Add repetitions before touching the dial.","Then load","Small increments, honestly logged.","Then density","Same work in less time is real progression.","The hinge anchor","Hip patterns set the week's training tone.","Rest as training","Strength arrives in the recovery window.","Two square metres and a pair of adjustable dumbbells out-train a garage of unused machines. The programme is the equipment; the weights are just the resistance.","x"],
["sports/how-psr-and-points-deductions-work","Where The Deductions Come From","Points deductions arrive when the accounts fail the sustainability test: losses beyond the threshold across the assessment window trigger sanctions, and the independent commission sets the scale. The table's oddities often start in the balance sheet.","The loss threshold","A fixed amount of losses across three seasons.","Sanction scales","The commission grades the breach, not the press release.","The amortisation route","Player sales rebalance a single window.","Promotion timing","Wage commitments arrive before the revenue does.","The appeal process","Mitigation arguments are heard before deductions stick.","Follow the accounting and the league table explains itself: every deduction is an arithmetic consequence wearing a sporting verdict's clothing.","x"],
["entertainment/reviews/the-black-book","What The Review Weighs","The Black Book gets its power from scale: production gloss, a revenge architecture and a streaming rollout that put Nollywood crime on global shelves. The craft questions are pacing and the second act's detours, and the review takes both seriously.","The production floor","Cinematography and sound at international streaming standard.","The revenge engine","A father's plot with political scaffolding.","Pacing under review","The second hour's detours are the real debate.","Streaming distribution","Platform reach rewrites the box-office maths.","The genre's growth","Crime thrillers travel across language markets.","Nollywood reviews work best as craft readings against infrastructure. The Black Book is the case study: a film whose ambitions are visible in every frame and whose faults are pacing's, not budget's.","x"],
["entertainment/french-new-wave-explained","Where To Start Watching","Start the New Wave with three films: one Godard for the grammar, one Truffaut for the heart and one Varda for the range. The movement's classics are short, sharp and stranger than their reputations suggest.","The jump cut","Godard's edits taught the medium to blink.","Location sound","Streets and cafés replaced studio silence overnight.","The auteur turn","Directors became signatures, not contractors.","Varda's range","The movement's widest lens belongs to her.","The influence stream","Every handheld drama owes the movement rent.","Watch the key texts and contemporary cinema explains its own rules back to you. The New Wave's innovations became invisible precisely because they won.","x"],
["writers/writing/zyzzyva","What The Magazine Publishes","Zyzzyva publishes fiction, poetry and essays with a distinctly West Coast attention to place and voice. The magazine's reading periods are announced on its channels, and its slush pile is read by people who remember every submission.","Fiction, poetry, essays","Three forms, one editorial voice.","The place lens","Landscape and city as co-characters.","Reading periods","The window opens on the magazine's own schedule.","Contributor pay","Accepted work is paid at stated rates.","The slush ethic","Small magazines read with human depth.","Rejection from a magazine like this is a normal year's work, and the reading itself is the tuition. Submit where the issues are worth reading first.","x"],
["tech/smr-vs-cmr-hard-drives","How To Tell Which Is Inside","The spec sheet tells the truth the box hides: SMR drives list their recording technology in fine print, and CMR drives cost more per terabyte for a reason. NAS rebuilds are where the difference becomes a week of waiting.","Track overlap","Shingled writes punish small random updates.","Rebuild week","RAID rebuilds expose SMR's worst hours.","The spec-sheet hunt","Recording technology lives in the fine print.","Archival fits SMR","Cold storage rewards capacity over write speed.","Databases want CMR","Continuous writes are the misbuy trigger.","Buy for the workload that writes the disk most: archival boxes save money with SMR, and anything rebuilding, logging or virtualising buys CMR.","x"],
["entertainment/best-anime-to-watch-now","How The Picks Were Made","The seven picks were chosen on three filters: complete seasons worth finishing, streams that are legitimately licensed, and first episodes that hook without homework. The list favours finishability over reputation.","Finishable runs","Complete arcs beat endless seasons.","Licensed streams only","Every pick plays on legitimate platforms.","First-episode hooks","The entry test is the pilot, not the ranking.","Genre spread","One per lane: action, romance, comedy, drama.","No homework","Standalone stories welcome newcomers first.","Anime curation is a choice problem: the medium's volume is the barrier, and seven trusted beats a hundred ranked.","x"],
["entertainment/why-everything-is-a-remake","When A Remake Earns Its Keep","A remake earns its keep when the new version adds context the original could not have: a different culture, a new technology or a story told from the shadow's point of view. Everything else is inventory management.","The awareness dividend","Known titles market themselves for free.","New context","Translation across cultures counts as craft.","The shadow's view","Same story, different centre of gravity.","The budget logic","Risk-averse money follows proven narrative.","The creative cost","Originals lose the slot the remake fills.","Audiences buy the familiar and keep the receipts: the remake wave is arithmetic. The exceptions are the films that found a new story inside the old title.","x"],
["writers/start","Where The First Week Goes","Spend the first week on three shelves: the writing basics for foundations, the paid-work guides for direction and the tools for momentum. One finished piece beats ten saved articles, and the site is arranged to produce exactly that outcome.","The basics shelf","Voice, structure, paragraphs and revision.","The paid-work track","Freelance routes and pricing guides.","The tools shelf","Calculators and checkers that clear busywork.","The learn index","Structured paths with a clear order.","Come back weekly","New guides land on a steady schedule.","The door is here so newcomers arrive at a finished piece rather than a reading list. Start at the basics and stop at the next draft.","x"],
["writers/writing/solarpunk-magazine","What Solarpunk Publishes","Solarpunk Magazine carries fiction, essays and art about futures with parts lists, and the editorial taste favours engineering optimism over escapism. The submission windows open on the magazine's own calendar, and rates are stated with the guidelines.","Futures with parts lists","Hope as a design problem, not a mood.","Fiction and essays","Speculative stories and their arguments.","Art pages","The magazine's visual side is part of the genre.","Stated windows","Submissions open on a published schedule.","Rates published","Payment terms live with the guidelines.","The genre takes solutions seriously as drama, and the magazines that carry it reward stories where the hopeful future has a bill of materials.","x"],
["entertainment/10-facts-about-agent-kim-squid-game-season-3","What We Know About The Role","Agent Kim's role grew from the season's design: the pink suit, the mask work and a performance the camera keeps finding. The verified details are production facts; everything else is fandom speculation, and the line between them is drawn here.","The costume design","The pink suit is the show's shorthand.","Mask and face","The performance lives in the eyes.","Screen time math","The reception outran the minutes.","The ensemble design","Every numbered player stays human.","Verified only","Production facts, dated and sourced.","Character listicles earn their keep by respecting the line between the show's text and the fandom's noise. This one stays on the production side of the line.","x"],
["entertainment/how-to-build-a-watchlist","The Purge Ritual","The watchlist fix is a purge ritual: cap the list at a season's viewing, delete what you will never start, and schedule the survivors one night per week. The deleted titles teach your taste faster than the kept ones.","The seasonal cap","One season of viewing is the honest shelf.","Delete freely","The purge is a taste-education exercise.","One night per week","Calendared viewing actually happens.","Mood sorting","Match the shelf to your actual evenings.","The rewatch slot","Comfort viewing deserves scheduled space.","A watchlist is a promise with limited hours attached. Size it to the calendar, and the graveyard becomes a wardrobe.","x"],
["home/harmattan-and-your-electronics","The Dust Season Calendar","The harmattan protocol is a calendar: covers on before the dust arrives, weekly vent cleans through the season, and power conditioning installed before the first generator surge. The month's maintenance buys the quarter's uptime.","Cover before dust","The season's first week sets the schedule.","Weekly vent care","Soft brushes and air, never vacuums.","Power conditioning","Surge protection earns its cost in one outage.","Static management","Humidify the room, ground the desk.","Screen protection","Microfibre only, dry, never sprayed.","Harmattan is a maintenance season wearing weather's clothes. The households that prepare in November stop buying replacements in February.","x"],
["entertainment/why-tv-seasons-are-getting-shorter","What The Short Season Changed","Short seasons changed television's texture: arcs get tighter, filler disappears and the hangout comedy loses the long afternoons it used to enjoy. The format's gains and losses are both real, and the audience feels them in different shows.","Tighter arcs","Eight hours demands a planned shape.","The filler loss","Standalone bottle episodes became rarer.","Showrunner models","Authorship rewards the compact season.","The comfort cost","Fewer hours with the characters we live with.","Limited series absorb the stories the twenty-two-episode season used to stretch, and the hangout comedy quietly lost its native habitat. Both halves of the change are in the catalogue.","x"],
["sports/how-football-scouting-works","Why The Layers Disagree","Scouting layers disagree productively: the scout's eye, the video room's role profiles and the model's shortlist see different truths. The clubs that recruit well keep every layer's confidence proportional to its evidence.","Live reports","Observers answer questions the club pre-wrote.","Video review","Clips judged against the role, not the highlight.","Model filters","Numbers narrow the field to the worth-watching.","Character work","Background checks decide more than talent reports.","Training trials","The ground reveals what film cannot.","The pipeline is expensive attention at its core. Recruit well and the layers argue toward the truth; recruit badly and the shortlist becomes a verdict.","x"],
["home/induction-hob-wiring","The Electrician's Checklist","The induction wiring checklist has four items: dedicated circuit, correct breaker rating, pan compatibility test and a consumer-unit capacity check. Households that run the checklist before buying avoid the renovation's most expensive stall.","Dedicated circuit","An oven-class draw needs its own line.","Breaker rating","The install guide's amperage is the floor.","Pan test","Bring your favourite pan to the showroom.","Panel capacity","Older boards may need the upgrade priced in.","The visible hob is half the decision. Price the wiring first, and the kitchen upgrade proceeds without the three-week electrician's gap.","x"],
["entertainment/movies-like-deadpool-and-wolverine","Why The Tone Balance Holds","The films that hold the tone balance care about their characters while winking at the genre. The picks here share that double vision: the joke lands because the stakes are real, and the violence choreographs like dance.","Caring while winking","Irony without heart is the failure mode.","Choreographed violence","Staged fights are comedy's straight man.","Cameo economy","Surprise guests reward the faithful.","Buddy engines","Mismatched partners bicker through apocalypse.","Meta comedy","The fourth wall is a tool, not a crutch.","Tone is the whole trick in this lane: the films that work love the genre enough to mock it precisely, and the audience feels the difference in the first scene.","x"],
["home/ceiling-fan-vs-standing-fan","The Noise Question","Noise is where ceiling fans win quietly: large blades at low RPM move air at lower decibels than any pedestal fan at full tilt. The standing fan answers with portability and the fact that renters can take it when they move.","Blade physics","Large and slow beats small and fast on noise.","Room coverage","A ceiling fan conditions the whole volume of air.","Renter portability","The standing fan's lease travels with it.","Winter mode","Reversed ceiling fans recirculate rising heat.","Installation cost","Wiring and height are the ceiling fan's tax.","The noise comparison settles bedrooms; the installation comparison settles rented rooms. Most households end up with one of each, placed by the room's job.","x"],
["sports/gegenpressing-explained","Where The Tactic Breaks","Gegenpressing breaks in three places: when the first press gets bypassed, when the fitness clock runs down, and when the opponent plays over the swarm rather than through it. The counter to the counter-press is the long ball and the cool head.","The bypass risk","A single line-break exposes the whole shape.","The fitness cliff","Pressing intensity decays across ninety minutes.","Playing over it","Long balls behind the press end the argument.","The six-second rule","Win the ball back or reorganise immediately.","Triggers, not shouting","Teams move on rehearsed cues.","The tactic is a bet on the moment after losing the ball. The teams that beat it treat that same moment as their attack's starting gun.","x"],
["home/heat-pump-vs-gas-furnace","The Hybrid Answer","The hybrid answer handles the cold edge: a heat pump for the ninety percent of the year at moderate temperatures, and a gas furnace for the design week when the mercury finds the floor. Dual-fuel controls switch automatically.","The design week","Size the backup for the coldest stretch, not the average.","Efficiency curves","Heat pump output falls as the temperature drops.","Fuel price math","The local tariff ratio decides operating cost.","Panel capacity","Heat pumps ask questions of old electrical panels.","Ductwork condition","Distribution changes every efficiency calculation.","Run the arithmetic on the coldest week rather than the year's average and the hybrid configuration usually prices itself into the answer.","x"],
["home/leaky-faucet-diy","When To Call Someone","The tap is DIY-safe until three signs appear: a corroded seat, a seized valve or a supply line that will not shut. Photograph every step before disassembly and the reassembly solves itself.","Isolate first","The water goes off before any tool moves.","Photograph the teardown","Phone photos make reversal foolproof.","The seat check","Pitted seats defeat every new washer.","Cartridge swaps","Modern taps hide ceramic internals.","Seized valves","Penetrating oil, patience, then the wrench.","A dripping tap is the perfect first repair: cheap, contained and immediately rewarding. The three warning signs are the whole boundary between homeowner territory and the plumber's.","x"],
["writers/writing/mudroom","What A Domestic Essay Needs","A domestic essay needs one room, one behaviour and one turn toward the larger world. Mudroom's taste runs to that exact structure, and the payment details live on the submissions page with the reading windows.","One room, one turn","The essay's scale shift is its whole architecture.","Precision of detail","The universal arrives through the specific.","Payment stated","The magazine publishes what it pays.","Reading windows","Submissions open on a stated calendar.","The archive teaches","Recent issues reveal the editorial eye.","Domestic writing earns its keep through precision: name the object, feel the weight, then look up. The magazine's shelf rewards exactly that discipline.","x"],
["entertainment/mission-impossible-watch-order","The Two Paths Compared","Release order rewards patience with the ensemble's slow chemistry build; the modern-run shortcut delivers the stunt spine in three sittings. Both paths work because the franchise's continuity is character rather than plot.","Release order","The team's chemistry compounds across films.","The shortcut run","Three modern films stand almost alone.","The stunt spine","Each film's set piece is the real continuity.","The ensemble track","The team is the series, not the lead.","Nothing is truly skippable except by time pressure. Choose the path that matches the evening's budget and the franchise delivers on both.","x"],
["tech/phone-overheating-causes-and-fixes","The Fix Stack In Order","The fix stack removes heat sources in order: stop the sustained load, kill the rogue app, unplug the fast charger, leave the case off and move to shade. The phone's throttle protects the battery, and every fix respects that design.","Stop the load","Gaming and cameras stack heat fastest.","Find the drain","Battery settings name the rogue process.","Charge slower","Lower wattage when the phone is already warm.","Case and shade","Passive cooling is the first tool.","Heat retires batteries early. The throttle is the phone's self-preservation instinct, and the household's job is removing the reasons it fires.","x"],
["tech/mobile-data-not-working","The Ten-Second Fixes First","Before any reset, run the ten-second fixes: balance check, airplane toggle, data toggle and a coverage glance. The destructive resets can wait until the cheap checks have failed, because they cost your saved passwords.","Balance and bundle","Expired data looks identical to a broken network.","The airplane toggle","A radio restart fixes more than expected.","Coverage glance","The status bar reports before any app does.","APN backup","Screenshot carrier settings before touching anything.","Resets cost","Network resets clear passwords along with faults.","Troubleshooting is triage with a price list. Work down the cost ladder and the mobile data fault usually resolves in the first three steps.","x"],
["tech/phone-charging-slow-cable-port","The Port Inspection","Port inspection finds the slow charging culprit half the time: lint packs the connector, the cable's power wires have thinned, or the brick negotiates below the phone's appetite. Look inside the port before buying anything.","Lint first","Pocket debris is the cheapest fix in electronics.","Cable swapping","The data cable hiding thin power wires.","Brick wattage","The charger sets the ceiling, not the phone.","Heat throttling","Warm phones charge slowly by design.","Slow charging is a three-party negotiation, and the inspection order finds the weakest speaker in ten minutes.","x"],
["writers/learn/professional-writing/how-to-write-a-business-letter","The Three-Paragraph Body","The business letter body runs three paragraphs: context, request, consequence. The action line names exactly what you want done by when, and the format blocks signal professionalism before the first sentence lands.","Context first","Why the letter exists, in two lines.","The request","Say exactly what you need, unabbreviated.","Consequence","What happens next, including timing.","The action line","A named task with a named deadline.","Format is the letter's first credential: the address block and subject line carry half the message before the prose begins.","x"],
["writers/writing/litmag-online","How The Reading Works","LitMag Online's reading is compression-first: the magazine takes short fiction that earns every line, pays on acceptance and follows stated word limits. The guidelines are enforced because the slush pile is read by humans with a schedule.","Pay on acceptance","Payment arrives when the story is taken.","Compression first","Flash and short fiction reward economy.","Stated limits","Word ceilings are enforced at the door.","The human pile","Editors read submissions at reading pace.","Publication records start at paying markets like this one: a hundred dollars, a byline and a bibliography line that lifts every later submission.","x"],
["writers/learn/research-sources/how-to-find-reliable-sources","The Research Log","The research log is the discipline that makes deadlines cheap: every fact carries its source URL, its date and its corroboration status. When the fact-check arrives three months later, the log answers in one search.","Source URL","Where the fact came from, recorded at capture.","Date stamps","Facts expire at different rates.","Corroboration state","One source is a claim; two make a fact.","The primary pass","Original documents outrank summaries.","Log first, trust second. The writers who keep provenance build the one asset that compounds across every deadline.","x"],
["writers/writing/hobart","How To Read The Taste","Hobart's taste is compression as aesthetic rather than constraint: short pieces that treat every sentence as load-bearing. Read two recent issues before submitting and the fit question answers itself.","Compression as style","The short form is the point, not the ceiling.","Contemporary voice","The magazine reads for the current moment.","Recent issues first","Taste is legible in any two issues.","Payment on acceptance","Stated rates for accepted work.","Compressed pieces that earn their every line find this shelf. The submission is doing everything in your control when the fit is visible.","x"],
["writers/learn/types-of-writing/how-to-write-a-product-description","The Specifics That Sell","Specifics sell because they are the only claims a buyer can verify in advance: materials, dimensions, care instructions and the honest limit of what the product does. One call to action survives; two cancel each other.","Verifiable specifics","Concrete details beat every adjective.","Benefits translated","Features become outcomes the buyer can picture.","The honest limit","Naming what the product is not for builds trust.","One action","A single next step, clearly marked.","Product copy is a translation job: specifications into lives. Write the outcome first and the description sells without hype.","x"],
["tech/android-custom-rom-gsid-risk","The Rollback Checklist","The rollback checklist is the flashing contract: restore image downloaded, bootloader relock path documented, banking apps tested and the data backup verified twice. Flash only when every box is ticked.","Restore image","Downloaded before any unlocking begins.","Bootloader path","The relock procedure, documented and understood.","App compatibility","Banking and work apps tested on the ROM.","Verified backups","Two copies, one of them off-device.","Custom ROMs traded bricking folklore for integrity checks, and the modern risk is app refusal rather than hardware death. The rollback checklist is the whole safety net.","x"],
["tech/wifi-extender-vs-second-router-nigerian-house","The One-Cable Fix","The one-cable fix beats every extenders' promise: run Ethernet or powerline to the dead zone and put a real access point there. One node at full strength out-repeats three nodes whispering.","Backhaul beats repeat","Wired rebroadcast at full strength.","Wall physics","Concrete and rebar punish 5GHz.","One network name","Roaming between nodes needs coordination.","Power cuts","The inverter's uptime decides the network's.","Extenders halve bandwidth by design; a second router on a wired backhaul restores it. Diagnose the dead zone first and the cable solves the rest.","x"],
["tech/http-status-codes-explained","The Codes That Own The Fault","Status codes assign fault ownership in one number: 4xx blames the request, 5xx blames the server, and 3xx asks for patience while the resource moves. Memorise five codes and the web's error language becomes plain.","200 is not done","Success codes still describe different states.","301 versus 302","Permanence changes every cache's behaviour.","404 navigation","Missing pages are a wayfinding problem.","503 patience","The server asks for a retry, not a bookmark.","Read the status line first and debugging becomes diagnosis: the code names who owns the problem before any log is opened.","x"],
["writers/learn/online-writing","The Formats' Shared Contract","Every digital format keeps the same contract: the headline promises, the opening pays the click and the structure survives the phone screen. Master the shared contract and the format switches become cosmetic.","Promise and payoff","Titles are debts the first paragraph must clear.","Phone-first structure","Paragraphs sized for the smallest screen.","The newsletter relationship","Inbox writing is a correspondence.","Measured in actions","Landing pages earn their keep in conversions.","The formats differ in surface and share a spine: respect the reader's time, honor the headline, and the toolkit transfers across every assignment.","x"],
["writers/tracker","The Five Columns That Matter","Five columns run the whole submission life: piece, market, sent date, due date and rights. The five-minute weekly review keeps every follow-up on time and every returned right visible for the next send.","Piece and market","One row per submission, nothing else tracked.","The due clock","Every send gets a diary date immediately.","Rights column","Reprints need to know what came back.","The patterns review","Career trends surface from honest data.","Submission tracking is the career's bookkeeping: five columns and one weekly hour replace every expensive tracker app with a subscription fee.","x"],
["writers/learn/writing-basics/how-to-read-like-a-writer","The Seam Hunt","Seam-hunting reading asks three questions of every paragraph: where does it turn, what does the sentence length do, and which word was chosen against its synonyms. The habit converts every book into tuition.","Find the turn","Where the piece pivots is where craft lives.","Rhythm audit","Sentence length patterns are pacing tools.","Word-choice swaps","Synonyms reveal the writer's real options.","Marginal notes","Annotated books become workbooks.","Reading this way costs some entertainment and returns a classroom on every commute. Writers who master it cannot waste reading time.","x"],
["home/water-heater-flush-how-to","The Anode And The Valve","The water heater's two-part care is the annual flush and the anode check: the drain valve clears the sediment and the anode rod quietly dissolves instead of the tank. The relief valve test is the safety habit that protects people.","Sediment drains","The annual hose clears the season's scale.","Anode inspection","The sacrificial rod is a cheap, vital replacement.","Relief valve test","The safety check that takes thirty seconds.","Thermostat honesty","Scald protection is a setting to verify.","The rumbling is sediment boiling at the tank's floor. One hour a year buys quiet, efficiency and years of tank life.","x"],
["writers/learn/structure-formatting/how-to-write-an-introduction","Rewrite It Last","Introductions are written first and rewritten last, because the piece's true opening only becomes clear at the end. The edit rule is simple: whatever the first two sentences do not earn, cut.","The stakes sentence","The reader's reason to continue lives here.","The promised payoff","The intro borrows against the conclusion.","Voice contract","Sentence one sets the register for the piece.","Cut on sight","Introductions shrink in every honest edit.","Draft the door first, rewrite it last. The finished piece knows its own opening better than the plan ever did.","x"],
