TOPUP_SECTIONS20['home/mistakes/streaky-windows-sunlight'] = _top20('home/mistakes/streaky-windows-sunlight', 'Why The Streaks Come Back', 'Streaks return because the glass dries before the squeegee finishes: sunlight, over-soaped water and a saturated cloth are the three causes, and they stack. The professional schedule follows the shade across the house, and the solution barely foams at all.', ['The evaporation race', 'Hot glass dries the solution mid-pass and leaves the tide mark behind.', 'The soap trap', 'Foam leaves film on the pane; two drops per bucket is genuinely plenty.', 'Cloth discipline', 'One clean edge per pane, refolded often, never reused dirty.', 'The tool choice', 'Small squeegees control their corners far better than wide ones.', 'The finish pass', 'A dry microfibre edge catches the final line every single time.', 'The seasonal plan', 'Harmattan dust demands more frequent and much lighter cleans overall.'], 'Window cleaning is a drying-time race dressed up as a scrubbing job, and every streak is the record of where the glass dried first. Cut the soap until the water barely foams, chase the shade around the house through the morning, keep the rubber blade sharp and dry, and work one clean edge per pane with a folded cloth that never goes back dirty. The households that treat the chore as scheduling rather than effort never see the streaks come back at all.')
